      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Systemic racism in housing and banking is a historical and ongoing pattern of discriminatory practices, not just individual prejudice. Redlining, for example, systematically denied mortgages and investment to Black and minority neighborhoods, artificially depressing property values. This historical disinvestment directly translates into modern wealth gaps, as housing equity is the primary driver of generational wealth in America. Therefore, the current disparities are not accidental; they are the predictable outcome of deliberately biased institutional policies.",
      "source": "target",
