    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So you're saying the \"myth\" argument isn't really a valid academic perspective to include if I want to stay accurate to how these systems actually work? I just don't want the kids to think I'm being one-sided if they hear different arguments in the news or from their parents. Is there any legitimate economic theory that doesn't rely on the systemic racism framework to explain these gaps?",
